# tg_mhd (CUDA FP64)  tgc_slip_cond_n256_re1000_drive0.2_bdrive0.2  N=256 Re=1000 h=1.23199712e-02 delta=3.16227766e-02 delta/h=2.566790 layers=128 written=22
# THE ENERGY BUDGET against wall distance. Per probe, one row per term: t, the term,
# its contribution to the BOX MEAN from each of the layers 0..21 (layer k: the nodes
# k cells from the nearest wall, the slab [(k-1/2)h, (k+1/2)h]) and from the rest of
# the box beyond them, so a row sums to the box average. Paper units: energies in
# v0^2, rates in k0 v0^3. With eK = |u|^2/2 and eM = |B|^2/2,
#   d eK/dt = lor + advK + pres + difK + injK - visc   (injK = u.F, -drive only)
#   d eM/dt = S + advM + difM + cmpM + injM - ohm   (injM = B.S, -bdrive only)
# lor = u.(j x B); S = B_i B_j d_j u_i; advK, advM = -u.grad eK, -u.grad eM;
# pres = -u.grad p, p = cs^2 rho/u0^2; difK = nu div(u x w); difM = eta div(B x j);
# cmpM = -|B|^2 div u + (u.B) div B; visc = nu |w|^2; ohm = eta |j|^2. The scheme is
# weakly compressible, so a layer's terms close only to a residual.
# row 'vol': each column's share of the volume
